<Base title="Get Help" description="Current program status, rider resource information and proposed crash-recovery assistance from GEAR Moto Foundation.">
<section class="inner-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Rider Support</div><h1>When the Road Changes,<br/><span class="accent">Community Matters.</span></h1></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap prose"><div class="program-callout"><strong>Applications are not open.</strong> GEAR has not opened a public gear, education, medical relief, or hardship grant application cycle. The information below summarizes proposed programs, not an offer or guarantee of funding.</div><h2>Which Program May Fit?</h2><p><strong>Gear</strong> is planned to help eligible riders obtain essential helmets and other protective equipment. <strong>Education</strong> is planned to support approved safety and riding courses. <strong>Assistance</strong> is being developed as a community and resource network connecting riders to welcoming groups, mental health information, substance-use recovery resources and independent service providers; it is not a GEAR treatment or grant program. <strong>Recovery</strong> will house proposed accident-related medical and financial relief, rehabilitation and rebuilding support.</p><h2>Assistance: Community &amp; Resource Connections</h2><p>Sometimes the most valuable help is finding a community or knowing where to turn. GEAR is developing a rider-centered resource network for welcoming riding groups, emotional well-being, sobriety and recovery support, and practical community services. The future directory will use documented listing criteria; no third-party organization is currently designated as an approved GEAR partner.</p><p><strong>Independent public resources you can use now:</strong></p><ul><li><a href="https://211utah.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Utah 211</a> — local community, housing, health and support-service navigation.</li><li><a href="https://findtreatment.gov/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">FindTreatment.gov</a> — an independent federal directory of mental health and substance-use treatment providers.</li><li><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/find-help/helplines/national-helpline" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">SAMHSA National Helpline</a> — confidential treatment referrals at 1-800-662-HELP (4357).</li><li><a href="https://988lifeline.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline</a> — call or text 988 for immediate emotional or mental health crisis support in the United States.</li></ul><p>These links are informational, not endorsements or GEAR-managed services. GEAR volunteers do not provide counseling, diagnosis, substance-use treatment or emergency response. For immediate danger or a medical emergency, call 911. Please do not send mental health histories or other sensitive records to GEAR by email.</p><h2>Program Questions</h2><p>Contact <a href="mailto:gear@gearmotofoundation.org">gear@gearmotofoundation.org</a> for Gear, <a href="mailto:educate@gearmotofoundation.org">educate@gearmotofoundation.org</a> for Education, <a href="mailto:assistance@gearmotofoundation.org">assistance@gearmotofoundation.org</a> for resource guidance, or <a href="mailto:recovery@gearmotofoundation.org">recovery@gearmotofoundation.org</a> for general Recovery program questions. Applications are not open. Do not send medical records, financial documents or other sensitive materials to any of these addresses.</p><h2>Proposed Rider Relief Review</h2><p>The draft Recovery medical policy describes objective review of financial need, verified accident-related patient responsibility, relevant coverage, and accident circumstances. It proposes different review pathways for ordinary public-road accidents and lawful, organized, controlled track or training activities.</p><p>The draft also distinguishes ordinary riding mistakes from materially dangerous public-road conduct. Decisions would be internal charitable eligibility determinations, not legal findings of accident fault. A qualifying controlled motorsports event would not automatically be excluded merely because the activity involves performance riding.</p><h2>How Medical Assistance Would Work</h2><figure class="editorial-photo"><img src="/images/motorcycle-crash-recovery-medical-bills-support.jpg" alt="Injured motorcycle rider reviewing medical paperwork at home with a supportive family member." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1672" height="941"/><figcaption>Recovery involves medical expenses, practical support and rebuilding after a crash. Illustrative image.</figcaption></figure><p>Potential eligible bills include verified deductibles, copayments, coinsurance, emergency care, rehabilitation, prescriptions and similar accident-related patient expenses. Direct payment to medical providers is preferred. The draft policy does not authorize unrestricted payment of an insurance plan's theoretical out-of-pocket maximum.</p><figure class="editorial-photo"><img src="/images/gear-moto-foundation-rider-recovery-support.jpg" alt="Illustrative injured motorcycle rider reviewing recovery paperwork with a supportive companion." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1672" height="941"/><figcaption>Rider recovery and support, shown illustratively; no services or awards are depicted as completed.</figcaption></figure><h2>Privacy Comes First</h2><p>We are not collecting medical records or hardship applications through general email. Please do not email accident reports, insurance documents, financial records, health information or other sensitive materials. Secure intake procedures, final eligibility criteria, funding limits and application dates will be announced if programs launch.</p><p>For general questions about the proposed Recovery and Rider Relief program, contact <a href="mailto:recovery@gearmotofoundation.org?subject=GEAR%20Recovery%20Inquiry">recovery@gearmotofoundation.org</a>. For resource-navigation questions under the separate Assistance pillar, use <a href="mailto:assistance@gearmotofoundation.org?subject=GEAR%20Assistance%20Inquiry">assistance@gearmotofoundation.org</a>. Do not email medical records, accident reports or financial documents.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn-red" href="mailto:recovery@gearmotofoundation.org?subject=GEAR%20Recovery%20Inquiry">Ask About Recovery</a><a class="btn btn-outline-dark" href="/programs/">Review Programs</a></div></div></section></Base>